      "valuation_insights": "Apple reported annual total revenue of $478.8 billion for fiscal 2026, up 15.1% from $416.2 billion in fiscal 2025, both measured by net sales tagged as RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax [C:revenue]. Operating income was $158.1 billion, yielding an operating margin of 33.0% for fiscal 2026 [C:operating_income]. Net income attributable to Apple was $132.2 billion [C:net_income], producing GAAP diluted EPS of $8.98 for the year [C:diluted_eps]. Return on average equity was strong at 142.3%, using fiscal 2026 and 2025 stockholders' equity balances [C:return_on_average_equity]. Total debt including current portion was $78.9 billion, giving a debt-to-equity ratio of 0.70 [C:debt_to_equity]. Free cash flow reached $136.1 billion (operating cash flow minus capital expenditures) [C:free_cash_flow].\n\nFor the latest quarter (Q4 2026), Apple posted revenue of $114.5 billion, a 12% increase year-over-year [C:quarterly_revenue]. Quarterly GAAP diluted EPS was $2.10, up 14% over the same quarter last year [C:quarterly_eps]. Using the closing price of $344.63 as of October 30, 2026, Apple’s trailing twelve-month P/E ratio is approximately 38.4 based on fiscal 2026 diluted EPS [C:pe_ratio].\n\nComparing operating margins on total revenue basis, Microsoft’s margin was 46.8% for fiscal 2026, Alphabet’s 32.0% for fiscal 2025 (calendar year), and Oracle’s 30.6% for fiscal 2026 [C:operating_margin_peers]. These peers have different fiscal year-ends and revenue definitions, but all use contract-based revenue tags, enabling a consistent comparison.\n\nInsight: Despite a 12% quarterly revenue increase, Apple’s capital expenditures notably declined from $12.7 billion in fiscal 2025 to $9.0 billion in fiscal 2026, marking a meaningful capex reduction trend while still generating significantly higher free cash flow [10-K L000139 and L000116 lines].",
